<dcterms:bibliographicCitation xml:lang='el'>https://helios.eie.gr/helios/bitstream/10442/18480/1/B90_sxinas_Serres.pdf</dcterms:bibliographicCitation>
<skos:note xml:lang='el'>https://bg.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%BE%D1%81_%D0%A1%D1%85%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%81 (λήμμα στα Ρωσικα). Μετάφραση στα αγγλικα: Nikolaos Theologou Schinas (Greek: Νικόλαος Θεολόγου Σχινάς) was a Greek explorer of Macedonia, military and engineer. He was born in 1844 and died in 1912. By order of the Greek Minister of War, he toured the Ottoman provinces of Thessaly, Epirus and Macedonia and left valuable notes on the ethnic picture in the region at the end of the 19th century.</skos:note>
